<title>AUSTRALIA: Biggest gains/falls for ASX 100 index in past month.</title>
<headline>Biggest gains/falls for ASX 100 index in past month.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is a list of the 10 largest gaining and falling stocks for Australian companies included in the Australian Stock Exchange's ASX 100 index for the month to July 18.</p>
<p>    Top 10 largest gains in month</p>
<p>						 Percent</p>
<p>Rank Name			 Price     change</p>
<p> 1  Macquarie Bank	    12.89	17.08</p>
<p> 2  Santos			 6.40	16.36</p>
<p> 3  Oil Search		   3.80	15.15</p>
<p> 4  Howard Smith		13.80	14.05</p>
<p> 5  Village Road-Pr	    3.70	13.85</p>
<p> 6  Publish Broadcst	   8.05	12.59</p>
<p> 7  Fletcher-Energy	    4.35	12.12</p>
<p> 8  National Mutual	    2.17	10.71</p>
<p> 9  Westfield Amer-N	   1.21	 8.04</p>
<p>10  Commonwealth BK	   16.25	 7.95</p>
<p>    Top 10 largest falls in month</p>
<p>						 Percent</p>
<p>Rank Name			 Price     change</p>
<p> 1  Goldfields		   1.25     -37.50</p>
<p> 2  Acacia Resources	   1.38     -21.20</p>
<p> 3  Newcrest Mining	    2.70     -19.40</p>
<p> 4  RGC			    4.19     -18.16</p>
<p> 5  Lihir Gold		   1.90     -16.67</p>
<p> 6  Plutonic Rsc		 3.80     -15.93</p>
<p> 7  M.I.M. Hlds		  1.77     -13.24</p>
<p> 8  Sthn Pac Pete		3.75     -12.79</p>
<p> 9  Sons Of Gwalia	     4.75     -12.04</p>
<p>10  QNI Ltd			2.39     -10.82</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
